  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- Studio outtake of an idea that later became the bridge section of the reworked \"Dancing In The Streets.\" [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **gd1975.07.23.studio.bershaw.t01-Bo'sBlues1**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd1975-07-23.140800.sbd.bershaw.flac1644** (recommended): soundboard; 1 songs; 7 min; rated 3/5 by 1 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- A second take of this material was recorded the next day [1]\n- The piece stood alone as its own composition a year before reaching live audiences in 1976, when the band toured again [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd1975-07-23.140800.sbd.bershaw.flac1644**: transferred by Alan Bershaw; source: source/lineage: studio reel-> ?-> Maxell MX-S 100 cassette with Dolby B; [1]",
